        "direction": "vertical",
        "gap": "sm",
        "padding": 16
      },
      "children": [
        "recommendation_title",
        "recommendation_body"
      ]
    },
    "recommendation_title": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "Recommendation for Sun-Seekers",
        "variant": "h3"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "recommendation_body": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "For a tourist who prefers warmer and sunnier conditions, Lisbon is the recommended choice for an October trip.\n\nWhile both cities boast a pleasant average high temperature of 22°C, Lisbon's key advantages are its warmer evenings and greater amount of sunshine. The average low in Lisbon is a comfortable 15°C compared to Rome's cooler 12°C, making it more pleasant for evening activities. Additionally, Lisbon typically offers an extra hour of sunshine per day. Although it has a slightly higher number of rainy days on average, the combination of warmer nights and more sun makes it the better option for your stated preferences."
      },
      "children": []
    },
